  "validation_notes": [
    "Full package suite passed, then malformed-cap coverage passed under race and the added RPC payload test passed separately. Runtime source is unchanged since implementation_source.",
    "The first race invocation passed all Go packages but its shell wrapper failed after an on-disk script edit. It is not counted as a successful invocation. An immutable wrapper rerun exited zero; race-first.* retains the original evidence.",
    "58,800 direct comparator pairs cover all five supported transaction types, nil/zero/nonzero base fee, negative and overflow caps. Nine frozen real-pool heap cases cover three permutations and three base-fee values.",
    "Heap arrays, exact comparator calls, Underpriced, Discard and failed-capacity rollback are differential checked against the normal comparator.",
    "RPC integration verifies the nested matrix, correlation fields, additive schema and cumulative counters. Recorder tests cover immutable payloads and overwrite/cursor-loss semantics.",
    "The example below has an intentionally injected mutex wait. Its wall times are a test trace, not a pinned benchmark or a production sample.",
    "Allocations vary with lookup-map ordering and comparison participation of SetCode transactions; allocation differences between separate processes are not exact instrumentation allocation counts."
  ],
